What is Bash?

Bash is a command-line shell.

A Bash script is a text file containing commands that can be executed as a script.

Example:

#!/bin/bash


echo "System Information"
date
whoami
hostname
Making a Script Executable
chmod +x script.sh

The +x adds execute permission.

Run the script:

./script.sh

It can also be run with:

bash script.sh
Why Use Bash Scripts?

Bash scripting can help automate repetitive tasks.

Examples:

Backups
Log cleanup
System information collection
Maintenance
File management
Monitoring tasks

Automation saves time and reduces repetitive manual work.

